# Run in an HTTP client with private variables; do not commit actual credentials.
@base = http://localhost:8080/api/v1

GET {{base}}/ready

### Authenticate CLI (token supplied by your HTTP client, not inline in this file)
GET {{base}}/technologies
Authorization: Bearer {{cli_token}}

### Transient search: never automatically saved
POST {{base}}/search
Authorization: Bearer {{cli_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"query":"Como ler CSV usando Pandas?","language":"pt-BR","preferred_sources":["official"],"ai_enabled":false,"technology":"pandas"}

### Explicitly save the complete response obtained above, without another search
POST {{base}}/saved
Authorization: Bearer {{cli_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"response":{{search_response}},"title":"Leitura de CSV"}

### Filter / paginate / sort
GET {{base}}/saved?page=1&page_size=20&technology=pandas&order=title
Authorization: Bearer {{cli_token}}

### Rename
PATCH {{base}}/saved/{{saved_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{cli_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Minha referência CSV"}

### Physical delete
DELETE {{base}}/saved/{{saved_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{cli_token}}

### Web login (same configured Origin)
POST {{base}}/auth/session
Origin: http://localhost:8080
Content-Type: application/json

{"password":"{{web_password}}"}

### Session-authenticated search
POST {{base}}/search
Origin: http://localhost:8080
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"query":"Como ler CSV usando Pandas?"}
